---
import SubPage from '../../layouts/SubPage.astro';
import { DOCS_SIDEBAR } from '../../lib/sidebar-data';

const currentPath = '/docs/install';
---

<SubPage
  title="Install · pace"
  description="Install pace plugins in Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini, Codex, and the Cowork desktop app. Two flows for engineers and non-technical users."
  activeNav="docs"
  canonicalPath={currentPath}
  sidebarLabel="Docs"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    {DOCS_SIDEBAR.map((group) => (
      <div class="subpage-sidebar-group">
        <span class="subpage-sidebar-group-title">{group.title}</span>
        <ul class="subpage-sidebar-list">
          {group.items.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={item.href}
                aria-current={item.href === currentPath ? 'page' : undefined}
              >{item.label}</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </Fragment>

  <article class="installpage">
    <header class="installpage-header">
      <span class="installpage-eyebrow">Get started</span>
      <h1>Install pace</h1>
      <p class="installpage-lede">
        Pace is a Claude Code plugin marketplace. Register the marketplace once, then install the plugins your team uses. Two install paths: <strong>Claude Code CLI</strong> for engineers, and the <strong>Cowork desktop app</strong> for everyone else.
      </p>
    </header>

    <nav class="installpage-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <span class="installpage-toc-label">On this page</span>
      <ol class="installpage-toc-list">
        <li><a href="#claude-code">Claude Code (engineers)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#cowork">Cowork (non-technical users)</a></li>
        <li><a href="#picking">Picking plugins</a></li>
        <li><a href="#pace-cli">The <code>pace</code> CLI</a></li>
        <li><a href="#updating">Updating</a></li>
        <li><a href="#verifying">Verifying it worked</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="claude-code">
      <h2>Claude Code (engineers)</h2>
      <p>
        If you already run Claude Code in your terminal, this is the canonical flow. Three commands, no config files to edit, no API keys to manage.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Register the marketplace</h3>
      <p>One-time per project. Tells Claude Code that <code>pace.tools</code> is a source of plugins.</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>claude plugin marketplace add pace.tools</code></pre>
      <p class="installpage-aside">
        Behind the scenes this fetches <a href="/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json">marketplace.json</a> and registers the 50 plugins it lists. You don't install all 50; you install the ones your team uses.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Install the plugins your team uses</h3>
      <p>Install one plugin per team or function. The router (<code>pace</code>) is optional but recommended; it's where your company-specific commands go.</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code><span class="installpage-comment"># The router (company commands like /pace teach)</span>
claude plugin install pace@pace.tools

<span class="installpage-comment"># Department plugins (install only what you use)</span>
claude plugin install sales@pace.tools
claude plugin install engineering@pace.tools
claude plugin install data@pace.tools
claude plugin install marketing@pace.tools</code></pre>
      <p>
        Not sure which to install? See <a href="#picking">Picking plugins</a> below, or jump to the <a href="/docs/teams">team guides</a> for role-based recommendations.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Connect your tools (on first use)</h3>
      <p>
        Plugins ship with connectors but they're not authorized yet. The first time you run a skill that needs Slack, HubSpot, Notion, or any other MCP server, Claude opens an OAuth flow in your browser. Sign in, approve, and the token is saved for next time.
      </p>
      <p>
        For the full connector model (OAuth, self-hosted URLs, local stdio servers), see <a href="/docs/connectors">Connectors &amp; MCP</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="cowork">
      <h2>Cowork (non-technical users)</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://cowork.com/">Cowork</a> is a desktop app that wraps Claude Code in a graphical interface. No terminal, no <code>npm</code>, no command-line install. Pace plugins are the same plugins; Cowork just installs them through clicks instead of commands.
      </p>

      <h3>1. Install Cowork</h3>
      <p>Download the desktop app from <a href="https://cowork.com/">cowork.com</a> and sign in with your Anthropic account. Cowork runs on macOS and Windows.</p>

      <h3>2. Add the pace marketplace</h3>
      <ol class="installpage-steps">
        <li>Open Cowork and go to the <strong>Plugins</strong> tab.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Add marketplace</strong>.</li>
        <li>Paste <code>pace.tools</code> as the marketplace URL.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Add</strong>. Cowork loads the catalog of 50 plugins.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>3. Install plugins by clicking</h3>
      <p>
        Browse the catalog inside Cowork and click <strong>Install</strong> next to each plugin you want. A salesperson installs <code>sales</code>; a product manager installs <code>product-management</code>; an HR person installs <code>human-resources</code>. The <a href="/docs/teams">team guides</a> have starter sets for every role.
      </p>

      <h3>4. Authorize connectors when prompted</h3>
      <p>
        The first time a skill needs an external tool (Slack, HubSpot, Notion, etc.), Cowork opens an OAuth window. Sign in, approve, and the connector stays authorized.
      </p>

      <div class="installpage-callout">
        <strong>One install, multiple users.</strong> If you're rolling pace out to a team of non-technical users, install Cowork once on a shared template machine, register pace, then have everyone sign in with their own Anthropic account. Each user authorizes their own connectors against their own accounts.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="picking">
      <h2>Picking plugins</h2>
      <p>
        Pace ships 50 plugins. Most teams install three to six. Two ways to pick:
      </p>

      <h3>By role</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href="/docs/teams">team guides</a> have starter sets for sales, marketing, engineering, data, product, design, finance, legal, operations, people, customer support, and productivity. Each guide lists the plugins to install and a sample week of commands.
      </p>

      <h3>By plugin</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href="/plugins">plugin catalog</a> shows every plugin with its skills, connectors, and intended audience. Browse it like an app store.
      </p>

      <p class="installpage-aside">
        Installing more plugins isn't free: each one adds skills to your <code>/</code> menu and bytes to the agent's context. Start with the few that map to your weekly work and add more as you find gaps.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="pace-cli">
      <h2>The <code>pace</code> CLI</h2>
      <p>
        Pace also ships a small Node CLI you can run with <code>npx</code>. It's an alternative to the Claude Code marketplace flow, useful in two cases:
      </p>
      <ul class="installpage-bullets">
        <li>You want the same skills installed across <strong>multiple AI harnesses</strong> in the same project (Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, etc.). The CLI copies into all of them at once.</li>
        <li>You want a <strong>scripted, repeatable install</strong> for onboarding new repos, dev containers, or CI.</li>
      </ul>

      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code><span class="installpage-comment"># Install pace skills into every detected harness</span>
npx pace skills install

<span class="installpage-comment"># Check if updates are available</span>
npx pace skills check

<span class="installpage-comment"># Update to the latest skills</span>
npx pace skills update

<span class="installpage-comment"># List every command pace ships</span>
npx pace skills help</code></pre>

      <p>
        Harness directories it writes into: <code>.claude</code>, <code>.cursor</code>, <code>.gemini</code>, <code>.agents</code>, <code>.github</code>, <code>.kiro</code>, <code>.opencode</code>, <code>.pi</code>, <code>.qoder</code>, <code>.rovodev</code>, <code>.trae</code>, <code>.trae-cn</code>. Only harnesses present in your project are touched.
      </p>

      <div class="installpage-callout installpage-callout-warning">
        <strong>What the CLI installs.</strong> <code>npx pace skills install</code> installs the <code>pace</code> router skills and offers to bring <a href="https://impeccable.style">impeccable</a> along for frontend design. It does <strong>not</strong> install the department plugins (sales, engineering, etc.); those are Claude Code marketplace plugins. Use <code>claude plugin install</code> for them, or install through the Cowork UI.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="updating">
      <h2>Updating</h2>

      <h3>Claude Code</h3>
      <p>Marketplace plugins update with the same command they install with:</p>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>claude plugin marketplace update pace.tools</code></pre>
      <p>That refreshes pace's catalog. Per-plugin updates land when Claude Code re-resolves the marketplace.</p>

      <h3>Cowork</h3>
      <p>Open the Plugins tab and click <strong>Check for updates</strong> on the pace marketplace. Cowork pulls the latest version of each installed plugin.</p>

      <h3>Pace CLI</h3>
      <pre class="installpage-pre"><code>npx pace skills update</code></pre>
      <p>Reads the latest skills from the GitHub source and refreshes every harness directory.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="installpage-section" id="verifying">
      <h2>Verifying it worked</h2>
      <p>
        Open a chat in Claude Code or Cowork and type <code>/</code>. You should see commands prefixed by the plugins you installed: <code>/sales:call-prep</code>, <code>/engineering:standup</code>, <code>/pace:teach</code>, etc. Type one and the corresponding skill takes over.
      </p>
      <p>
        Connectors stay <em>declared but not authorized</em> until the first skill that needs them runs. That's by design: authorization is just-in-time, so a fresh install doesn't barrage you with OAuth windows you don't need yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Stuck? Open an issue at <a href="https://github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/pace.tools/issues">github.com/GoldenBerry-SO/pace.tools</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SubPage>

<style>
  .installpage {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .installpage-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .installpage-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .installpage-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .installpage-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .installpage-lede a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-toc {
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }
  .installpage-toc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px var(--spacing-md);
    counter-reset: toc;
  }
  .installpage-toc-list li {
    counter-increment: toc;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list li::before {
    content: counter(toc, decimal-leading-zero) ' ';
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    margin-right: 4px;
  }
  .installpage-toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart), border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list a:hover {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-color: var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-toc-list code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .installpage-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .installpage-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .installpage-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .installpage-section p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .installpage-section ol,
  .installpage-section ul {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .installpage-section li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .installpage-section a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .installpage-section a:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-section strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .installpage-pre {
    background: oklch(18% 0.015 150);
    color: oklch(92% 0.005 150);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-pre code {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .installpage-comment {
    color: oklch(62% 0.04 150);
  }
  .installpage-aside {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-style: italic;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-mist);
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-left: 2px;
  }
  .installpage-aside a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .installpage-callout {
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-forest);
    padding: var(--spacing-md) var(--spacing-lg);
    border-radius: 0 6px 6px 0;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .installpage-callout strong {
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .installpage-callout-warning {
    background: var(--color-clay-dim);
    border-left-color: var(--color-clay);
  }
  .installpage-callout-warning strong {
    color: var(--color-clay-hover);
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .installpage-toc-list {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
